# eoreader6.1 · kernel · turn 002 — supersedes gap-002
# Act: NUL*  (Void aimed at Pattern)   Stance: Unraveling   Site: Kind
#
# gap-002 refused this act for lack of a second occurrence to re-enter on.
# That gap is not deleted — it is superseded, because what it was missing
# now exists: kernel/data/signal-a.json and kernel/data/signal-b.json are
# two INDEPENDENTLY generated series (different seeds, kernel/GOAL.md)
# that each carry a genuine structural absence (null, not a low-magnitude
# sample) at the same site-role — index 16 of 32, the midpoint.
#
# The pattern claim, stated exactly: the SAME KIND of absence recurs at
# the SAME structural site across two grounds that share no material —
# this is not turn-1 restated (a different series, a different seed), it
# is the re-entrant reading gap-002 required. Per Decal Notation's
# composition table, `*` is the operator meeting its own prior output;
# here that output is "an absence was found at relative index 16," and
# this turn is what happens when that finding is checked against an
# independent second instance of itself rather than repeated on faith.
#
# The negative control, checked and not just asserted: kernel/data/
# noise-control.json is the same construction with NO absence planted.
# NUL+ must find nothing there. If it did, the recurrence claimed here
# would be indistinguishable from a kernel that sees figures everywhere —
# eoreader6's own mandatory-negative-control discipline (SEED.md
# Amendment XIV), carried forward rather than skipped because this is a
# new codebase. This also retroactively strengthens turn-001: a single
# hand-picked target address (customer:123.preferred_contact) is now
# joined by a real instance checked against a real negative control,
# rather than resting on one illustrative example alone.
#
# Refuted if: a third independently-generated series with an absence at a
# DIFFERENT site-role is later found, and this kernel cannot tell the
# difference between "recurs at the same site" and "recurs anywhere" —
# that would mean this turn mistook coincidence for kind, exactly the
# failure `patternSpaceAdmissible`-style admissibility checks exist to
# catch in eoreader6's own statistics. Not yet tested; recorded as an
# open refutation condition rather than assumed clear.

:turn-2  eot:opens         :turn-1 .
:turn-2  eot:supersedes    :gap-002 .
:turn-2  eot:act           eot:NUL* .
:turn-2  eot:stance        "Unraveling" .
:turn-2  eot:site          "Kind" .
:turn-2  eot:reenters      :turn-1 .
:turn-2  eot:evidence      "kernel/data/signal-a.json" .
:turn-2  eot:evidence      "kernel/data/signal-b.json" .
:turn-2  eot:control       "kernel/data/noise-control.json" .
:turn-2  eot:site_role     "index:16 of 32 — midpoint" .
:turn-2  eot:witnessed     true .
:turn-2  eot:closes        [ eot:aperture 1.0 ; eot:perturbation "none" ] .
